  "notes": "The compiler builds the whole tree since ontology round R10 (gate round 10, one or more objects moved at once): B2b-tokens-enter-that-many-counters, a ZoneChangeEvent (ANY -> BATTLEFIELD YOU, subject a token you control) with once_per_event, one trigger for the tokens one event moves (CR 603.2c: one instruction's tokens, the objects one atom boundary journals, GameEvent.batch). 'That many' is QProp(event, THAT_MANY_COUNT), the number of tokens the event gathered, the ones that left before the ability resolves included (the card's ruling). Closes the needs-atom of 2026-11-05 (a batched zone-change trigger whose 'that many' is the batch size). Packs tools/scenarios/mapped/M20/woodland_champion_two_tokens_at_once.json (Raise the Alarm's two Soldiers: one trigger, 2 counters; Ferocious Pup's Wolf: a second) and woodland_champion_three_zombies_at_once.json (Undead Servant's three Zombies: 3 counters; the opponent's tokens: none); the trigger counts and a token leaving before resolution in MTG_bot/core/test_executor_one_or_more.py."
